<title>BELGIUM: EU Commission adopts green rate compensation.</title>
<headline>EU Commission adopts green rate compensation.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A draft regulation to compensate British, Irish and Italian farmers hit by revaluation of national currencies will limit European Union payments to seven per cent of income lost, a Commission official said on Friday.</p>
<p>EU farm support payments are calculated at the so-called agricultural conversion or green rate which falls when the strength of national currencies rises.</p>
<p>&quot;The draft regulation adopted on Wednesday will fix direct income aids such as beef premia but compensation for loss of incomes is limited to seven per cent of the amount,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The regulation covers compensation for loss of income due to reductions in intervention (market support) prices and export refunds to be 50 percent financed by the European Union.</p>
<p>Other member states are already covered by similar legislation. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
